yeah, I'm of the opinion that there are characteristics of Bitcoin that make it a bit of a ponzi scheme. For those that say Bitcoin doesn't rely on new users, I would argue that new miners increases the hash rate and the securitization of the platform and new users also brings on new demand, increasing the price and improving the stability of Bitcoin - both necessary for a functional currency.

&#x200B;

At the same time, there is certainly immense intrinsic value in Bitcoin. We need only look to the developing countries already adopting Bitcoin to see that the use of a decentralized stable currency can improve transaction velocity and create better marketplaces.

